      "message": "Please update the docs to be similar to the rest of the package: explain what we do and add `.See RFC 4253, Section x.x.` at the end. \n\nAlso add a note explaining that for compatibility with existing clients (specifying the affected putty and ssh.net versions), we also accept short signatures for rsa-sha2 variants, but we may remove this support in the future because RFC 8332 says they are not allowed, even though a verifier can still accept them. Also add a reference to the OpenSSH code that accepts the short signature so we can easily check if this is changed in the future.\n\nThank you!",
